+### Inferences
+- **Revenue ranking (all estimates):** Calm (~$210M) > Headspace (~$140M) >> Insight Timer (~$20–30M) ≈ Finch (~$12M) ≈ Waking Up (~$8–9M iOS, more including web and Android) > Hallow, Open, Balance, Happier (undisclosed).
+- Insight Timer is plausibly the third-largest pure meditation business by revenue and the largest by free audience. Waking Up is the closest premium challenger.
+- Valuations across the category have collapsed (Headspace went from $3B to about $0.3B), and funding has stalled: Open's last round was in 2021, Happier's in 2018. Insight Timer's profitability on modest capital (about $30–40M raised) is unusual in the category.
+
+### Gaps
+- No company-reported 2025–2026 figures were found for Waking Up, Happier, Balance, Open or BetterSleep.
+- Business of Apps pages returned 403, so Calm and Headspace estimates rest on the earlier notes.
+- No successor to David Ko at Calm was found.
+
+## 4. Content model and library size
+
+### Takeaway
+Insight Timer is the only open marketplace of teachers, with 300,000+ tracks from about 20,000 teachers. Every other app is curated:
+- **In-house plus celebrity:** Calm (about 100+ Sleep Stories).
+- **In-house, clinical framing:** Headspace (500+ meditations).
+- **Founder voice plus a named roster:** Waking Up, Plum Village, Dan Harris's new app.
+- **Studio instructors:** Open.
+- **Algorithmically assembled from recorded fragments:** Balance.
+
+Medito and Smiling Mind are small curated libraries (Smiling Mind about 700 sessions).
+
+### Cited Findings
+- **Calm:** "100+ exclusive Sleep Stories, new content added every month" — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/calm/id571800810). The standalone Calm Sleep app advertises 500+ Sleep Stories — [Sacra](https://sacra.com/c/calm/). Calm has moved into video with an HBO Max series — [Sacra](https://sacra.com/c/calm/). Sleep Stories remain human or celebrity narrated — [ai_landscape notes](https://techcrunch.com/?p=3045822).
+- **Headspace:** "over 500+ guided meditations", sessions from 3 minutes upward, plus therapists and coaches — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/headspace-meditation-sleep/id493145008).
+- **Waking Up:** Sam Harris as creator, plus about 25 named teachers and guests, including Joseph Goldstein, Diana Winston, Adyashanti, Henry Shukman, Alan Watts (archival), David Whyte, Oliver Burkeman, Matthew Walker, Yuval Noah Harari, Michael Pollan, Jack Kornfield and Loch Kelly. "Every practice, course, and teacher is chosen" — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/waking-up-meditation-wisdom/id1307736395). A June 2026 program, Deep Rest Reset, was built with scientist Andy Galpin — [Fitt Insider press release](https://insider.fitt.co/press-release/waking-up-launches-recovery-program-with-dr-andy-galpin/).
+- **Happier:** "world-class teachers", none named on the listing — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/id992210239). Its original anchor voice, Dan Harris, left in 2024 — [Business Wire, 2024-09-10](https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20240910036070/en/Ten-Percent-Happier-App-Rebrands-to-Happier).
+- **Balance:** daily sessions assembled from "thousands of files" — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/-/id1361356590).
+- **Open:** an "endless library" with fresh classes daily; no instructors named on the listing. One reviewer says older videos are reused in programs — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/open-breathwork-meditation/id1482725254).
+- **Medito:** library size not stated ("dozens of categories") — [Medito Foundation](https://meditofoundation.org/free-meditation-app/).
+- **Smiling Mind:** "over 700 sessions and 90 collections and pathways" — [Smiling Mind app page](https://smilingmind.com.au/smiling-mind-app).
+- **Plum Village:** 100+ guided meditations and 300+ videos, a single-lineage voice (Thich Nhat Hanh and monastics) — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/-/id1273719339).
+- **BetterSleep:** stories "created in-house or inspired by existing tales", with a creative content producer writing all the sleep narratives — [BetterSleep blog](https://www.bettersleep.com/blog/10-questions-with-a-creative-content-producer-aster-j-haile).
+- **Healthy Minds:** "up to 600 days" of content built on Richard Davidson's Center for Healthy Minds research — [hminnovations.org](https://hminnovations.org/?p=6858).
+- **Meditopia:** 1,000+ guided sessions (an app-library description) — [ORCHA/Macmillan app library](https://macmillanapplibrary.orchahealth.com/focus-area-mental-health/app-collection-mental-health-mindfulness-and-relaxation).
+
+### Inferences
+- Insight Timer's library is roughly 500–600 times Headspace's by track count, but it is uncurated. Competitors sell curation ("chosen", "expert-led") as the antidote to Insight Timer's breadth.
+- Balance's "assembled from fragments" model is the closest existing analogue to generated or personalised sessions (relevant to Aurelia). It shows that consumers will pay $70 a year for "a session built for me", even without generative AI.
+
+### Gaps
+- No verified library counts for Waking Up, Open, Happier or Medito.
+
+## 5. Personalisation and AI features
+
+### Takeaway
+No major competitor generates guided audio with AI. AI is used for:
+- **Chat:** Headspace's Ebb, Insight Timer's Reflect.
+- **Recommendations and plans:** Calm search and Calm Sleep plans, Insight Timer intentions.
+- **Fragment assembly:** Balance, pre-LLM style personalisation.
+
+App Store listings for Waking Up, Happier, Open, Medito, Smiling Mind and Plum Village mention no AI. Headspace under Sword is the competitor most likely to push AI hard.
+
+### Cited Findings
+- **Headspace Ebb.** An "empathetic AI companion" offering personalised recommendations — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/headspace-meditation-sleep/id493145008).
+  - Launched late 2024 — [eMarketer](https://www.emarketer.com/content/headspace-cuts-13--of-its-workforce--transitions-staff-therapists-contract-part-time-roles).
+  - Trained in motivational interviewing. In May 2025 it became the core of Headspace's "stratified care" offer for organisations, and regular users showed 34% higher engagement — [Business Wire, 2025-05-21](https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250521958749/en/Headspace-Unveils-Stratified-Care-Model-Powered-by-Empathetic-AI-Companion-Ebb) (from earlier notes).
+  - Sword plans AI for early need detection and clinician routing — [MobiHealthNews](https://www.mobihealthnews.com/news/sword-health-acquire-headspace-all-cash-deal).
+- **Calm.**
+  - Personalised search based on preferences and listening history (2024) — [TechCrunch, 2024](https://techcrunch.com/?p=2843535) (search summary).
+  - Calm Sleep builds a personalised sleep plan (Sept 2025) — [TechCrunch, 2025-09-16](https://techcrunch.com/2025/09/16/calm-launches-standalone-ios-app-for-sleep-support).
+  - No AI feature on the US App Store listing — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/calm/id571800810).
+  - Ko linked his departure to AI ("if we weren't having AI conversations today, I'd still be the CEO") — [Fast Company, 2026-04-07](https://www.fastcompany.com/91522961/why-calm-ceo-david-ko-is-stepping-down-after-scaling-the-meditation-app) (via search).
+  - Products listed as "Calm AI" on Product Hunt and similar directories appear to be third-party apps, not Calm's — [Product Hunt](https://www.producthunt.com/products/calm-ai/launches).
+- **Balance.** Personalisation from mood and goal inputs, which improves "as users share more"; the listing does not mention AI — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/-/id1361356590).
+- **BetterSleep.** The listing describes a "patented AI-powered algorithm" for playback of stories and sounds. No evidence was found of generated stories — [BetterSleep, App Store](https://apps.apple.com/app/id314498713) (search summary).
+- **Generated-content rivals (adjacent).** Welltory's Sleep Flow plays AI-generated stories that adapt to heartbeat — [VKTR](https://www.vktr.com/the-wire/welltory-launches-first-personalized-ai-generated-bedtime-stories-driven-by-users-heartbeats). Loftie offers unlimited AI-personalised bedtime stories — [Loftie](https://learn.byloftie.com/personalized-bedtime-story-and-meditation-membership-for-better-sleep). Endel generates soundscapes; see the earlier notes.
+- **Smiling Mind.** "Personalised" means search, filters and a custom Routine; no AI — [Smiling Mind app page](https://smilingmind.com.au/smiling-mind-app).
+- **Insight Timer, for contrast.** Reflect (AI chat) and a January 2026 AI intention recommender exist, but content is "No AI" — [Insight Timer AI safety](https://insighttimer.com/ai-safety); [GlobeNewswire via Manila Times, 2026-01-06](https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/01/06/tmt-newswire/globenewswire/insight-timer-launches-new-years-resolution-and-intention-setting-features-with-ai-recommendation-engine/2253735).
+
+### Inferences
+- Insight Timer and Headspace are level on AI chat. Insight Timer is ahead of Calm on AI in the product, and behind Balance on per-person session assembly.
+- No incumbent generates sessions. Whoever does it first at scale is likely to be Headspace/Sword, given the AI-first acquirer, or a small startup. The Calm CEO's AI-linked exit hints that Calm faces a strategic AI decision.
+
+### Gaps
+- No primary Calm statement on generative AI was found.
+- No details found of Balance's algorithm or of any AI features at Waking Up, Happier or Open.
+
+## 6. Notable 2024–2026 moves, and what users praise or complain about
+
+### Takeaway
+2024–2026 was a period of consolidation and retrenchment:
+- Headspace cut staff, then sold to Sword for about a tenth of its peak value.
+- Ten Percent Happier rebranded to Happier, its founder left and launched a rival app.
+- Calm diversified (Calm Sleep, Calm Health, retail tie-ins) while its revenue fell and its CEO departed.
+- Waking Up kept shipping premium programs.
+
+Complaints about paid apps centre on billing and auto-renewal. Complaints about free apps centre on depth and engagement.
+
+### Cited Findings
+**Moves**
+- **Headspace.**
+  - Cut 13% of its workforce in late 2024 and moved staff therapists to a flexible network from 2025-03-15 — [eMarketer](https://www.emarketer.com/content/headspace-cuts-13--of-its-workforce--transitions-staff-therapists-contract-part-time-roles).
+  - Ebb launched (late 2024) and became the core of stratified care (May 2025); see section 5.
+  - Sword acquisition (2026) and post-deal layoffs (Oct 2026) — [Behavioral Health Business, 2026-10-16](https://bhbusiness.com/2026/10/16/headspace-issues-layoffs-following-sword-health-acquisition/).
+- **Calm.**
+  - 2024: personalised search; story-like mindfulness exercises pitched as an alternative to social media — [TechCrunch, 2024-08-28](https://techcrunch.com/2024/08/28/calms-new-story-like-mindfulness-exercises-offer-an-alternative-to-social-media/).
+  - April 2025: "Not Calm Moms" maternal mental-health program.
+  - September 2025: the standalone Calm Sleep app.
+  - October 2025: a Lifestyle hub with partner brands (Nissan, AllTrails).
+  - December 2025: Target bedding with a free Premium subscription; a Hilton partnership.
+  - January 2026: Calm Health joined Solera.
+  - February 2026: annual price rise — [Sacra](https://sacra.com/c/calm/).
+  - Calm Sleep launch date: [Calm press release](https://blog.calm.com/blog/calm-sleep-press-release).
+  - Android XR app — [Calm blog](https://www.calm.com/blog/calm-android-xr) (undated).
+  - CEO Ko stepping down (April 2026); see section 3.
+- **Ten Percent Happier → Happier.** Rebranded on 2024-09-10. Co-founder Dan Harris left, kept the podcast and took full ownership of it on 2025-03-01 — [Business Wire, 2024-09-10](https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20240910036070/en/Ten-Percent-Happier-App-Rebrands-to-Happier). Harris launched the rival app "10% with Dan Harris" in December 2025 and said the name may change within about 18 months for legal reasons — [podcast episode, 2025-12-19](https://www.podbean.com/ew/dir-ph2nv-29a71785); [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/10-with-dan-harris/id6755701096). Happier also ran a free-subscription offer aimed at "bad meditators" — [Athletech News](https://athletechnews.com/happier-app-lures-bad-meditators-free-subscription/) (date not captured).
+- **Waking Up.** A 2025 NYT Wirecutter pick and a 2026 App of the Day; an iOS 27 "Liquid Glass" redesign (Nov 2026) — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/waking-up-meditation-wisdom/id1307736395). Deep Rest Reset with Andy Galpin launched June 2026 — [Fitt Insider](https://insider.fitt.co/press-release/waking-up-launches-recovery-program-with-dr-andy-galpin/).
+- **Smiling Mind.** A redesigned app rolled out from July 2024 and reset users' progress data — [Smiling Mind FAQ](https://www.smilingmind.com.au/smiling-mind-changing-faq).
+- **BetterSleep.** Bundled into Teladoc's cardiometabolic program in April 2025 — [Teladoc, 2025-04-08](https://www.teladochealth.com/newsroom/press/teladoc-health-introduces-next-generation-cardiometabolic-health-program).
+- **Balance.** Continuing (or ending) the "free first year" promotion; see section 2.
+- **Wirecutter.** Its August 2025 newsletter "Our new favorite meditation app" describes a pick with "the largest library of meditations available for free" and daily-intention prompts — [newsletter mirror, Aug 2025](https://kafficecco.blogspot.com/2025/08/our-new-favorite-meditation-app.html). The app is not named in the retrieved text, but the description fits Insight Timer (my inference). Waking Up also carries a "2025 Pick by NYT Wirecutter" badge — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/waking-up-meditation-wisdom/id1307736395).
+
+**Praise and complaints**
+- **Calm and Headspace.**
+  - Billing and auto-renewal are the top complaints: charges after cancellation, an $80 annual charge after a short trial, slow support (Trustpilot reviews 2025–2026) — [Trustpilot: Calm](https://www.trustpilot.com/review/calm.com?page=6); [Trustpilot: Headspace](https://au.trustpilot.com/review/headspace.com?page=5).
+  - Some Headspace users who came through insurance or employer access found the content and interface underwhelming — [Trustpilot CA: Headspace](https://ca.trustpilot.com/review/headspace.com?page=4).
+  - Aggregator analyses (low authority) agree that content quality is praised and billing criticised — [bigideasdb](https://bigideasdb.com/headspace-vs-calm-user-frustrations-2026); [marlvel.ai](https://marlvel.ai/intel-report/health-fitness/calm).
+  - Headspace praise: help with anxiety and sleep, and the Apple Watch panic button. Requests: AirPlay, longer walking audio — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/headspace-meditation-sleep/id493145008).
+- **Open.** Praise: high-quality instructors, accessible breathwork, Oura integration, responsive support. Complaints: vague class titles, intensity mislabelled, limited movement variety, reused videos — [App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/open-breathwork-meditation/id1482725254).
+- **Medito.** Praise: everything free, no sign-up. Complaints: shorter sessions, no guided timer — [Selfpause](https://www.selfpause.com/resources/medito); [Google Play](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=meditofoundation.medito&hl=en_US) (from earlier notes). Engagement is low: 18.9% still using after 14 days — [JMIR 2026](https://mhealth.jmir.org/2026/1/e79366).
+
+### Inferences
+- Insight Timer has avoided the Calm and Headspace billing backlash; it historically sends trial-end reminders (see the earlier notes). That gives it a trust advantage worth keeping as it tests paywalls.
+- The Happier split shows the risk of a founder-voice brand. Waking Up's value is tied to Sam Harris in the same way, and Insight Timer's marketplace spreads that risk across many teachers.
+
+### Gaps
+- No review-roundup scores (Verywell, Healthline) were retrieved for 2026.
+- No 2024–2026 news was found for Open, Balance, Plum Village (the press release returned 503) or Medito.
+- No evidence found of Calm layoffs in 2024–2026; the 20% cut was in 2022.
+
+## 7. How each compares with Insight Timer (free vs paid, human vs AI, breadth vs depth)
+
+### Takeaway
+Insight Timer sits in a unique corner: free and very broad, human-made through a marketplace, and cheap at the paid tier. Competitors beat it on:
+- **Curation and depth:** Waking Up, Plum Village.
+- **Clinical and enterprise reach:** Headspace, Calm Health.
+- **Sleep specialism:** Calm, BetterSleep.
+- **Per-person session assembly:** Balance.
+- **Zero paywall:** Medito, Smiling Mind.
+
+The clearest gap no one fills is a session generated for one person's moment, which Insight Timer has chosen not to build.
+
+### Cited Findings
+- See the citations in sections 1–6. The comparison grid below draws only on them (US prices, fetched 2026-11-16, unless noted).
+
+| App | Annual / monthly (US) | Free tier | Content model | AI | Scale signal | Owner |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Insight Timer | $59.99 / $9.99 | 300k+ tracks free | ~20k-teacher marketplace | Reflect chat; AI recs; "No AI" content | 32M+ members (claim); ~350k subs; ~$20M subs rev 2023 | Insight Network (independent) |
+| Calm | $69.99 app / $79.99 web; monthly $14.99–16.99 | small sampler | in-house + celebrity | recs/search; no gen AI | ~$210M rev 2025 (est.); 180M downloads | independent (VC) |
+| Headspace | $69.99 / $12.99 | limited | in-house, clinical | Ebb AI companion | ~$140M rev (est.); ~2M subs (est.) | Sword Health (2026) |
+| Waking Up | $149.99 (also $199.99 SKU) / $19.99 | ~5 sessions (user claim); scholarships | founder + curated roster | none listed | ~$700k/mo iOS (est.) | Waking Up Course LLC |
+| Happier | $99.99 / $9.99–14.99 | not stated | in-house teachers | none listed | 143K ratings | Happier Meditation Inc. |
+| Balance | $69.99 / $11.99; lifetime $399.99 | trial; "free year" (conflicting) | assembled fragments | personalisation, not labelled AI | 121K ratings | Elevate Labs |
+| Open | $149.99 / $19.99 | trial | studio instructors | none listed | $14.5M raised (2021) | Open Inc. |
+| BetterSleep | ~$9.99–99.99 SKUs | limited | in-house sounds and stories | "AI-powered" playback | ~1.3M MAU (est.) | Teladoc |
+| Medito | free | everything | small curated set | none | 4.1M+ downloads | nonprofit (NL) |
+| Smiling Mind | free | everything | curated, 700+ sessions | none | 9M+ people | nonprofit (AU) |
+| Plum Village | free | everything | single lineage | none | 140k–500k+ (conflicting) | nonprofit |
+| Healthy Minds | free | everything | research-led programme | none | ~500K installs (est.) | nonprofit |
+
+### Inferences
+- **Free vs paid.** Insight Timer wins against every paid app except on curation. Against Medito, Smiling Mind and Plum Village it has the much bigger library, but it carries a paywall those apps lack, and gated content draws backlash (see `users_backlash.md`).
+- **Human vs AI.** Every major player keeps its content human. Headspace and Insight Timer use AI for conversation, Calm and Insight Timer for discovery, and Balance for assembly. "Human-made" is not a differentiator against Calm, Waking Up or Plum Village. It differentiates only against generated-content entrants.
+- **Breadth vs depth.** Insight Timer is the breadth extreme. Waking Up and Plum Village are the depth extreme and command the highest price (Waking Up). The beginner middle ground (Headspace, Calm, Balance) sells a guided path, which is the thing Insight Timer users say they lack.
+- **Gaps in the market:**
+  1. Truly per-person sessions: Balance comes nearest, and nobody generates them.
+  2. Outcome-tracked progress: Smiling Mind's mood tracking and Calm Sleep plans are partial attempts.
+  3. Clinical routing for consumers, away from employers: Headspace and Calm Health focus on enterprise.
+  4. A billing-trust brand at the $70 price point.
+
+### Gaps
+- No head-to-head retention data (D30, churn) for any app except the Medito study.
+- Android prices and web prices were not checked.
