+<tr><td><b>Waking Up</b></td><td>$149.99/yr, $19.99/mo</td><td>Founder plus a curated roster</td><td>None listed</td><td>~$700k/month on iPhone (est.)</td><td>Wins on depth; a sleep and recovery programme since June 2026</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Happier</b></td><td>$99.99/yr</td><td>In-house teachers</td><td>None listed</td><td>Rebranded from Ten Percent Happier in 2024; its founder left to start a rival app</td><td>Wins on “meditation for sceptics”</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Balance</b></td><td>$69.99/yr; $399.99 lifetime</td><td>Sessions assembled from ~8,000 recorded pieces</td><td>Personalised by rules, not labelled AI (<a href="https://balanceapp.com/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Balance</a>)</td><td>121K ratings</td><td>The closest to “made for you”, but no generation</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Open</b></td><td>$149.99/yr</td><td>Studio instructors, breathwork</td><td>None listed</td><td>$14.5M raised (2021)</td><td>Wins on breathwork and premium feel</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>BetterSleep</b></td><td>~$9.99–99.99</td><td>In-house sounds and stories</td><td>“AI-powered” playback only</td><td>~1.3M monthly users (est.); owned by Teladoc</td><td>Wins on sleep sounds</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Medito</b>, <b>Smiling Mind</b>, <b>Plum Village</b>, <b>Healthy Minds</b></td><td>Free</td><td>Small curated sets, nonprofits</td><td>None</td><td>Medito 4.1M+ downloads; Smiling Mind 9M+ people</td><td>Wins on “no paywall at all”</td></tr>
+</tbody></table></div>
+<h3>The AI apps that generate sessions</h3>
+<p>Making a session from a mood with an AI voice is now a <b>crowded but shallow</b> niche: a long tail of small apps with no disclosed funding.</p>
+<div class="rs-table"><table><thead><tr><th>App</th><th>What it does</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead><tbody>
+<tr><td><b>SoulWave</b></td><td>Writes a script with an AI model and voices it with ElevenLabs; first session in “about two minutes” (<a href="https://www.soulwaveapp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">site</a>)</td><td>Not stated</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>ELYND</b></td><td>Generated guided sessions from how you feel (<a href="https://elynd.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">site</a>)</td><td>$11.99/mo, $69.99/yr</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Rosebud</b>, <b>Mindsera</b>, <b>Stoic</b></td><td>AI journaling and reflection: text, not audio</td><td>$99.99–129/yr</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Wysa</b>, Headspace <b>Ebb</b></td><td>AI chat for mental health, moving into care providers</td><td>Mostly through employers</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Endel</b></td><td>Generates soundscapes, not spoken guidance; $22.1M raised, now doing artist deals (<a href="https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/primary-wave-partners-with-endel-to-create-sleep-and-focus-soundscapes-from-artists" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MBW</a>)</td><td>$2.99–19.99/mo</td></tr>
 </tbody></table></div>
-<p>Nobody well funded makes <b>a new session from one sentence, refined with modular changes, inside an adaptive journey</b>. That is still open.</p>
+<div class="rs-split">
+  <div class="rs-no"><b>Crowded</b><ul><li>Big libraries of recorded meditations</li><li>AI journaling and AI chat coaches (also the riskiest legally)</li><li>One-off “mood → generated meditation”</li></ul></div>
+  <div class="rs-yes"><b>Still open</b><ul><li>Changing one part of a generated session and keeping the rest (our “Lego” changes)</li><li>A journey that learns from the person’s own check-ins</li><li>Generated audio that is clearly labelled and crisis-aware, offered as a reason to trust it</li></ul></div>
+</div>
+<p><b>What this means for Aurelia:</b> generating a session is not a moat on its own; any developer can wire an AI model to a voice. The moat is what happens after: the change-one-thing loop and the per-person learning. The biggest threat is still a large app (Calm, or Headspace under Sword) adding generation to an audience it already has. No well-funded player ships the full loop today.</p>
